<p>The UK RMG entered the first of a ppossible five 10-day confirmation periods yesterday. Should it remain above +5 per cent for each of these periods, the UK's green rate will revalue on 20 August 1997. On the basis of exchange rates from 1-2 July, the RMG for the UK is greater than + 5 per cent at +5.828. it is therefore currently forecast to enter a second confirmation period on 11 July. All currencies with negative RMGs for the period will be devalued on 11 July by reducing their gaps to zero. Hence, devaluations are currently forecast for the green rates of Belgium, Denmark, Holland, France, Germany, Spain, Portugal and Austria. During confirmation periods the 3-day (6 per cent) rule is suspended.</p>
